WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.275
(upbeat string music)

00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:07.358
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:24.522
- [Narrator] We all know that everything

00:00:24.522 --> 00:00:26.350
tastes better deep-fried.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.260
But what if I told you that in Thailand,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.427
the same goes for flowers?

00:00:31.551 --> 00:00:33.623
Eating flowers goes back generations

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:35.491
to when other foods were scarce

00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:38.491
and today, can be found
in both luxury restaurants

00:00:38.491 --> 00:00:40.574
and street vendors alike.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.691
One such island where you can find

00:00:43.691 --> 00:00:48.141
these crispy beauties is Koh
Kret, just outside Bangkok.

00:00:48.141 --> 00:00:52.224
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:55.462
Boonrod has been selling

00:00:55.462 --> 00:00:59.315
fried flowers in Koh
Kret for over 10 years.

00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:00.889
The flowers she sells are harvested

00:01:00.889 --> 00:01:04.886
from her very own garden as
well as those of her neighbor's.

00:01:04.886 --> 00:01:06.565
And her morning starts early.

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:10.648
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:24.491 --> 00:01:25.922
Some of the flowers you can find

00:01:25.922 --> 00:01:29.293
in Boonrod's shop are butterfly pea,

00:01:29.293 --> 00:01:31.158
bougainvillea and Ixora.

00:01:31.158 --> 00:01:35.241
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:45.545 --> 00:01:48.366
At 73 years old, Boonrod
is the oldest vendor

00:01:48.366 --> 00:01:50.798
selling fried flowers on the island.

00:01:50.798 --> 00:01:53.456
But she isn't protective
of her original recipe

00:01:53.456 --> 00:01:55.889
for the travelers who come to Koh Kret.

00:01:55.889 --> 00:02:00.402
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:02:00.402 --> 00:02:02.040
And also because Boonrod knows

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.864
her fried flowers are
just plain delicious.

00:02:04.864 --> 00:02:08.947
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:02:10.826 --> 00:02:12.793
You can bet that we'll be back for more.

00:02:12.793 --> 00:02:15.960
(upbeat string music)

